WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/telemetry/components/SignalStatsPanel.tsx — a PURE presentational leaf fed a computed
  `stats: SignalStat[]` prop (plus optional `selectedSignals` / `title` / `signalIndex` and a `loading` flag)
  by its parent (the Workspace / Explorer page). Regions:
    GlassPanel(p-4 sm:p-5) -> header row [ span.section-title{title ?? "Stats Summary"}
                              + Toggle "Hide empty ({{count}})" shown only when emptyCount > 0 ]
                           -> loading ? a grid of 4 Skeletons (grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4)
                           -> visibleStats.length > 0 ? DataTable(compact) with FIVE columns:
                                Signal (CHART_COLORS[idx] mono name, "No data in range" subtitle when empty),
                                Min, Max, Avg, Count. Min/Max = text-secondary, Avg = text-primary,
                                Count = text-muted; a NaN / non-finite value renders the muted "—".
                           -> else "No stats available".
  Behaviour: displayStats = selectedSignals ? one row per selected signal (gap-filled with emptyStatRow that
  shows "—" + "No data in range", new Map(stats) = last-wins) : stats. emptyCount = rows with count===0.
  visibleStats = hideEmpty ? drop empties : displayStats. Data sources: `useTranslation` only (no data hooks).
  Formatting helpers consumed: fmtNumber / fmtInt (numberFormat.ts, global precision 2, safeNumber => 0).
  i18n keys (t calls): Signal, Min, Max, Avg, Count, Stats Summary, No stats available,
  signalStats.noDataInRange, signalStats.hideEmpty.

